<title>USA: Bayer unit to plead guilty to price fixing.</title>
<headline>Bayer unit to plead guilty to price fixing.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Justice Department said Wednesday that Bayer AG's U.S. subsidiary has agreed to plead guilty and pay a $50-million fine for taking part in an international conspiracy to fix prices and allocate sales for citric acid.</p>
<p>It also said that Hans Hartmann, a senior executive at the German-based Haarman &amp; Reimer, another Bayer subsidiary linked to the U.S. unit, also has agreed to plead guilty for his role in the conspiracy.</p>
